# ── Cloudflare Turnstile (bot protection on contact + careers apply forms) ────
# Free, no quota. Create a widget at https://dash.cloudflare.com -> Turnstile
# -> Add site (Widget mode: "Managed" is a good default). Add your production
# domain (and localhost for local testing). VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is public
# and ships to the browser; TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY must stay server-only.
#
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION: api.contact.ts / api.careers.apply.ts fail closed
# (reject with an error, never accept the lead) when TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is
# missing in production, and always reject a missing/invalid token in
# production - see isProduction() in src/lib/turnstile.ts. The only bypass
# is local development / Vercel preview without a secret key configured, so
# contributors aren't forced to provision a widget just to run the app.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAAxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=0x4AAAAAAAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Resend (email delivery for contact form) ──────────────────────────────────
# Get your key at: https://resend.com/api-keys
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Site URL (used for sitemap, canonical URLs, email templates) ──────────────
# Set to your production domain without trailing slash
VITE_SITE_URL=https://ethixweb.com

# ── Vercel Blob (resume uploads for the Careers application form) ─────────────
# Created automatically when you add a Blob store to your Vercel project,
# or via: npx vercel env pull (after `vercel blob store add`)
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Supabase (durable lead records + AI candidate screening) ──────────────────
# Run every file in supabase/migrations/ once, in order, in a new Supabase
# project's SQL editor (see supabase/README.md), then get these from Project
# Settings -> API. Use the *service role* key, not the anon key - every table
# has RLS enabled with no anon policy on purpose. Without these set, the
# contact/careers-apply forms still work via email only (no durable record),
# and the AI screening endpoints are unavailable.
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Get your key at: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Optional - defaults to claude-sonnet-5 if unset
ANTHROPIC_SCREENING_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Random long string - signs the approve/reject links in the reviewer email
# so they can't be forged. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SCREENING_ACTION_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Where scored results + approve/reject links get emailed (Amar/Disha)
SCREENING_REVIEWER_EMAIL=you@ethixweb.com

# ── ClickUp (lead capture - contact form submissions become tasks) ────────────
# Personal API token: ClickUp -> avatar -> Settings -> Apps -> API Token.
# Every contact-form submission is mirrored as a task in the Leads list
# (Team Space > Ethixweb > Leads), auto-assigned for follow-up. Without these
# set, the form still works (email + Supabase only) - the ClickUp step is
# skipped with a warning in server logs.
CLICKUP_API_TOKEN=pk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
CLICKUP_LEADS_LIST_ID=901615913246
# Optional - comma-separated ClickUp user ids to auto-assign new leads to.
# Defaults to Amar only (see src/lib/clickup.ts).
# CLICKUP_LEADS_ASSIGNEES=95288619

# ── Gemini (AI assessment platform - question generation ONLY) ────────────────
# Get your key at: https://aistudio.google.com/api-keys
# Powers /careers/assessment (40-question proctored exam). Scoring is fully
# deterministic server-side - Gemini never sees candidate answers.
GEMINI_API_KEY=AQ.xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Optional - defaults to gemini-3.5-flash if unset
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# Where completed assessment reports (scores, answers, violations, recording
# links) get emailed. Falls back to info@ethixweb.com if unset.
ASSESSMENT_HR_EMAIL=you@ethixweb.com

# ── Google Ads Assessment (standalone, single-candidate, single-use exam) ─────
# Reuses RESEND_API_KEY, SUPABASE_URL/SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, and
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN above - no separate provider credentials needed. The
# 40-question exam is static/hand-authored (src/lib/gads-questions/), so this
# feature does not call Gemini or any other AI at exam time. There is no
# admin dashboard or login - the one link is created locally via
# `node --env-file=.env scripts/create-gads-invite.mjs` (see that file).

# Where the completed report (scores, written answers, violations,
# recommendation, PDF attached) gets emailed. Falls back to info@ethixweb.com
# if unset.
GADS_RECRUITER_EMAIL=you@ethixweb.com
